I've done item 1 of @yuanhao's decision on #1026: the JSON output and stream-json now both say when a reply was cut off or refused. Committed as e2354eee. fmt, clippy with -D warnings, the full cargo test run and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed for users:
• `--output-format json`: the result object has a new incomplete field. It is null for a normal ending. For a cut it is {"reason":"output_limit","limit_set_by":"default"} or {"reason":"output_limit","limit_set_by":"user"}, and for a refusal {"reason":"refusal"}.
• `is_error` was wrong before this fix: it only looked at whether the run failed. So a reply cut at a limit you never set, or a refusal, exited 1 while still reporting "is_error": false. It now matches the exit code in all four cases. Like external_servers (#895), this is a new field; is_error keeps its meaning.
• `--output-format stream-json`: now prints the same stderr line the text modes print (the output-limit warning or the refusal notice). Both modes call one shared printer, so the wording can't drift apart. Stdout is still JSON lines only.

Tests (in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs, using the real binary against the stub server):
• JSON, on both the -p and piped-stdin entry points: four rows (default-limit cut, --max-tokens cut, refusal, normal end), each checking incomplete, is_error, the exit code and that the partial answer is still in the object.
• stream-json: the same four rows, checking the note appears on stderr exactly once and every stdout line parses as JSON.
• One unit test checks that is_error and incomplete agree with the exit code, without running the binary.
• I broke each new piece on purpose, ran the tests and restored it in one command. With the JSON field disabled, the JSON test failed by name (left: Null). With the stream-json refusal note removed, the refusal row failed. Neither note printed before this change.
• I changed one existing test, test_build_json_output_structure_completeness, from expecting 9 top-level keys to 10, and it now also checks incomplete is null.

Not changed: the is_error written to the audit usage log still only looks at whether the run failed, so it can disagree with the JSON for a cut or a refusal. That was outside this task.

Docs: single-prompt.md has a table of the new field and describes the stream-json note, and ARCHITECTURE.md has a new entry. prompt.rs grew to 3,987 lines, so I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs to match. No "tracked in #1026" pointers were left to retarget, so pushing this commit closes #1026 cleanly.
